==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|breathe|er}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/bɹiː.ðə(ɹ)/}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːðə(r)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Something or someone that [[breathe]]s.
# A short [[break]]; a [[rest]] or [[respite]].
#: {{ux|en|After a short '''breather''' she was ready to continue up the hill.}}
# {{lb|en|physics}} A [[spatially]] [[localized]], time-periodic [[excitation]] in a one-dimensional [[lattice]].
# {{lb|en|colloquial|dated}} That which puts one [[out of breath]], such as [[violent]] [[exercise]].
# {{lb|en|mechanics}} An air inlet path to the [[crankcase]]

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|short break}} {{l|en|hiatus}}, {{l|en|moratorium}}, {{l|en|recess}}; see also [[Thesaurus:pause]]

